{
  "_comment": "Tide Island, restyled toward hypr/DESIGN-SPEC.md. Read by tide-island's UserConfigBackend from ~/.config/tide-island/userconfig.json. Keys and defaults come from backend/UserConfigBackend.cpp; anything omitted keeps its upstream default. Values that DIVERGE from upstream are the ones carrying spec intent, and each is noted in hypr/DESIGN-SPEC.md.",

  "_geometry": "Spec says 150x38. That number was measured off the video author's 2560x1440 display, where it is 5.9% of screen width. On this 1366x768 panel the same 150px is 11% - proportionally almost double, which is why it read as oversized. Scaled to the spec's PROPORTION instead of its pixel count: 5.9% of 1366 = 80, rounded up to 96 so the 24-hour clock keeps comfortable side padding.",
  "_height": "28, NOT the spec's 38. This is a deliberate user override of DESIGN-SPEC.md, recorded in REQUIREMENTS.md item 1: qtile's top bar was `bar.Bar(..., 28)` and that was the known-good daily driver for years, so it wins over a number measured off a stranger's 1440p screen. The width stays 96, so shrinking the height while keeping it is itself part of the padding fix - the clock gets smaller inside a box that does not.",
  "islandWidth": 96,
  "islandHeight": 28,
  "_notch": "islandTopMargin is now the FLOATING form's gap only. The resting form is the NOTCH: flush to the top edge, top corners square, a concave flare each side. That is a fork change in DynamicIslandWindow.qml (notchProgress / notchSkirt), not a config key - UserConfigBackend is compiled and has no notion of it. This value still matters because it is what the morph interpolates back to when notch mode is switched off.",
  "islandTopMargin": 11,
  "islandPositionX": 50,

  "_exclusiveZone": "The notch is flush at the top and 28 tall, so 28 is the minimum that keeps windows out from under it. 38 keeps the extra 10 as breathing room below the flares, which read badly with a window edge jammed against them - and 38 is also exactly what qtile reserved, since its 28px bar carried margin [5,10,5,10]. This shape IS the whole top surface; there is no separate bar to account for.",
  "islandExclusiveZone": 38,

  "_opacity": "Spec is emphatic that the shape is hardcoded #000000 and NOT theme-tinted: it is imitating bezel, and 'tint it and it stops being a notch and becomes a colored blob'. Upstream default 60 is translucent, so this is a real divergence. Theming goes INSIDE the island, never on the shell shape.",
  "islandBackgroundOpacity": 100,

  "_resting": "Spec's resting state is exactly two things: the clock and a 4-bar EQ that animates only while music plays. Workspaces, tray, battery and Wi-Fi are deliberately deleted - 'it earned permanent screen real estate by being occasionally relevant. That's a terrible trade.' Auto-hide is off because the pill is meant to be permanently present, not summoned.",
  "islandAutoHideEnabled": false,
  "islandShowWorkspaceOnAutoHide": false,

  "_expansion": "Spec: expands on hover, or click to pin. Media and notifications explicitly do NOT expand it - they swap the content while the shape stays put ('different mechanism entirely'), which is what disableAutoExpandOnTrackChange buys.",
  "hoverExpandAction": 1,
  "disableAutoExpandOnTrackChange": true,

  "_typography": "Spec substitutes Inter for SF Pro Text and Inter Display for SF Pro Display, with Inter Medium for body weight. inter-font provides both cuts from one Inter.ttc, and fc-match resolves all three names to themselves - verified, because a wrong family name silently becomes Noto Sans CJK with no warning.",
  "heroFontFamily": "Inter Display",
  "timeFontFamily": "Inter Display",
  "textFontFamily": "Inter Medium",
  "iconFontFamily": "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font",
  "_fontSizes": "Matched to qtile's widget_defaults, which set fontsize 10 - pango points at 96dpi, so ~13px on screen. The resting clock renders at bodyFontSize+1 (SwipeLyricsLayer), so bodyFontSize 12 puts it at 13 and lands on qtile's number exactly. title and icon follow the same ratio down from 20/18. The previous 20/16/18 in a 38px shape was proportionally the same as this - the island was simply a uniformly larger object than the bar it replaced, which is what read as oversized.",
  "titleFontSize": 15,
  "bodyFontSize": 12,
  "iconFontSize": 13,

  "_clock": "24-hour, matching hyprlock.conf's `date +%H:%M`. Upstream defaults to 12.",
  "clockFormat": "24",

  "_wallpaper": "The island ships its own wallpaper picker, which answers qtile's WallpaperPopup (9 bindings) without a port - it just needs pointing at the library, or it opens and says 'No wallpapers found'. 362 images live in ~/Pictures/Wallpapers. wallpaperPywalEnabled stays FALSE on purpose: AtiScriptsV1/theme-apply already owns pywal for both sessions and hypr/scripts/wallpaper-sync.sh feeds hyprpaper from the same cache, so enabling it here would give two independent things opinions about the same wallpaper and the qtile session would drift.",
  "wallpaperLibraryPath": "@HOME@/Pictures/Wallpapers",
  "wallpaperPywalEnabled": false
}
